+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Rust staticlib crates/ghostty-iroh (docs/IROH.md). OPTIONAL: nothing here is
+# used unless IROH=1 and the crate is present, and nothing below has been built
+# or run -- these are the pins the crate is to be built with, not evidence that
+# it builds. docs/iroh-build-wiring.md.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Fedora 44 packages, pinned by exact NEVR like BUILD_PKGS_PINNED and installed
+# into the build container by the same install_pinned. Fedora ships the
+# cross std (rust-std-static-x86_64-pc-windows-gnu), so no rustup is needed.
+# Observed available via `dnf repoquery` in fedora:ghostty-build on 2026-09-22;
+# not installed there yet.
+RUST_VERSION=1.98.1
+RUST_PKGS_PINNED="\
+rust-1.98.1-1.fc44 \
+cargo-1.98.1-1.fc44 \
+rust-std-static-x86_64-pc-windows-gnu-1.98.1-1.fc44"
+RUST_WINDOWS_TARGET=x86_64-pc-windows-gnu
+# The crate's own pin, for a reader who expects every revision to be in this
+# file. The authority is crates/ghostty-iroh/Cargo.lock, which the build uses
+# with --locked; this records which iroh release that lock is built around.
+# Empty until the crate lands.
+IROH_VERSION=
+# The dependency tree, `cargo vendor`-ed once and published as a single
+# sha256-pinned tarball -- the LUA_URL/LUA_SHA256 idiom, for the same reason:
+# the build must not reach the network. tools/fetch-vendor.sh unpacks it into
+# vendor/cargo, which is the shared Incus cache volume inside the build
+# container and is deliberately NOT part of the rsynced source
+# (tools/build-remote.sh push_source), so the large tree never crosses the
+# wire on every build. Empty = not published yet; fetch-vendor.sh skips it and
+# a cargo build would resolve online and say so.
+CARGO_VENDOR_URL=
+CARGO_VENDOR_SHA256=
+
 # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Incus build container (tools/build-container.sh, tools/build-remote.sh).
 # Heavy builds run in a container, never on the gaming PC. docs/BUILDING.md.
